 {"id": "PEDS-U279", "ch": 33, "n": 2, "title": "Modified Jones Criteria (2015)", "sec": "Jones criteria · p149", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-013", "PEDS-C33-014", "PEDS-C33-015", "PEDS-C33-016", "PEDS-C33-017", "PEDS-C33-018", "PEDS-C33-019", "PEDS-C33-020", "PEDS-C33-021", "PEDS-C33-022", "PEDS-C33-023", "PEDS-C33-024", "PEDS-C33-025", "PEDS-C33-026"], "guide": "Major (moderate–high risk): 1. pancarditis (clinical or subclinical ECHO+); 2. arthritis (mono/polyarthritis/polyarthralgia); 3. subcutaneous nodules; 4. erythema marginatum; 5. Sydenham's chorea. Low risk: only polyarthritis counts as major. Minor (moderate–high / low risk): arthralgia mono/poly; fever ≥38 / ≥38.5; ESR ≥30 / ≥60 mm/hr and/or CRP ≥3 mg/dl; PR interval listed only for moderate–high risk."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U280", "ch": 33, "n": 3, "title": "Essential Criteria & Diagnosis", "sec": "Essential criteria · p150", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-027", "PEDS-C33-028", "PEDS-C33-029", "PEDS-C33-030", "PEDS-C33-031", "PEDS-C33-032", "PEDS-C33-033", "PEDS-C33-034", "PEDS-C33-035", "PEDS-C33-036"], "guide": "Essential (preceding streptococcal infection): elevated ASO titer (preferred); throat swab culture (false +/− → not preferred); history of preceding sore throat (< 50%). Diagnosis + essential criteria: first episode — 2 major OR 1 major + 2 minor; recurrence — 2 major OR 1 major + 1 minor OR 3 minor."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U281", "ch": 33, "n": 4, "title": "ARF — Carditis", "sec": "Carditis · p150", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-037", "PEDS-C33-038", "PEDS-C33-039", "PEDS-C33-040", "PEDS-C33-041", "PEDS-C33-042", "PEDS-C33-043", "PEDS-C33-044", "PEDS-C33-045", "PEDS-C33-046", "PEDS-C33-047", "PEDS-C33-048", "PEDS-C33-049", "PEDS-C33-050", "PEDS-C33-051", "PEDS-C33-052"], "guide": "m/c feature of ARF (90%); early finding (within 2 weeks); all 3 layers → pancarditis; most serious (permanent valve damage). Pericarditis: chest pain + friction rub. Valvular m/c → mitral (F > m) > aortic (m > F): mitral valvulitis → Carey Coombs murmur (delayed diastolic); mitral regurgitation → soft S1, pansystolic murmur, hemodynamic overload → LVF (morbidity/mortality in ARF)."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U282", "ch": 33, "n": 5, "title": "ARF — Arthritis", "sec": "Arthritis · p150", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-053", "PEDS-C33-054", "PEDS-C33-055", "PEDS-C33-056", "PEDS-C33-057", "PEDS-C33-058", "PEDS-C33-059", "PEDS-C33-060"], "guide": "Large joints (knee, ankle, elbow) migratory arthritis; early finding, 30–50% of affected children; excellent response to aspirin; complete recovery (no residual joint damage)."},
