 {"id": "PEDS-U284", "ch": 33, "n": 7, "title": "Sydenham's Chorea", "sec": "Sydenham's chorea · p151", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-075", "PEDS-C33-076", "PEDS-C33-077", "PEDS-C33-078", "PEDS-C33-079", "PEDS-C33-080", "PEDS-C33-081", "PEDS-C33-082", "PEDS-C33-083", "PEDS-C33-084", "PEDS-C33-085", "PEDS-C33-086"], "guide": "Last manifestation (3 months after onset); semi purposeful jerky movements of limbs → abnormal coordination & posturing; associated: hypotonia, emotional lability, jerky speech; milkmaid grip sign (alternate tightening/loosening of grip); darting tongue sign (uncontrollable sliding in & out of tongue on protrusion); self resolving (2–6 weeks); if not resolving — diazepam, haloperidol."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U285", "ch": 33, "n": 8, "title": "ARF — Treatment & Secondary Prophylaxis", "sec": "Management · p151", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-087", "PEDS-C33-088", "PEDS-C33-089", "PEDS-C33-090", "PEDS-C33-091", "PEDS-C33-092", "PEDS-C33-093", "PEDS-C33-094", "PEDS-C33-095", "PEDS-C33-096", "PEDS-C33-097", "PEDS-C33-098", "PEDS-C33-099", "PEDS-C33-100"], "guide": "Treatment: bed rest for 2 weeks; penicillin — Inj. Penicillin G (Benzathine) single dose OR oral Penicillin V 250 mg QID × 10 days OR if allergic erythromycin 450 mg QID × 10 days; anti-inflammatories (steroids/aspirin). 2° prophylaxis: Benzathine/Penicillin G >30 kg: 12 lakh IU every 3 weeks; <30 kg: 6 lakh IU every 2 weeks; oral Pen V 250 mg BD; if allergic erythromycin 250 mg BD."},
 {"id": "PEDS-U286", "ch": 33, "n": 9, "title": "Anti-inflammatories & Duration of Prophylaxis", "sec": "Anti-inflammatories · p152", "qs": ["PEDS-C33-101", "PEDS-C33-102", "PEDS-C33-103", "PEDS-C33-104", "PEDS-C33-105", "PEDS-C33-106", "PEDS-C33-107", "PEDS-C33-108", "PEDS-C33-109", "PEDS-C33-110"], "guide": "Anti-inflammatory (for 12 weeks): steroids preferred (esp. cardiac problems) — oral prednisolone (2–40 mg/kg/day) × 3 weeks → taper over 9 weeks; aspirin 90–120 mg/kg/day in 4 divided doses × 10 weeks → taper over next 2 weeks. Prophylaxis duration: no carditis — next 5 years or till age 18 (whichever longer); carditis (without RHD) — next 10 years or till age 25 (whichever longer); established RHD/undergone surgery — till age 40 (ideal: life long)."},
